+<h1>Licence (EULA)</h1>
+<p><strong>Version 1.0, effective 22 November 2026</strong></p>
+<p>This agreement is between you (the person who bought or uses the software) and <strong>Muhammad Khizar, an individual trading as RageRun Games, of Karachi, Pakistan</strong> ("RageRun Games", "we", "us").</p>
+<p>It covers RageRun Vertical Shorts Editor, including its updates, files and documentation (the "Software"). By installing or using the Software you agree to this EULA. If you don't agree, don't install it, and ask for a refund under our Refund Policy.</p>
+<h2>1. Licence</h2>
+<p>When you buy the Software, we give you a personal, non-exclusive, non-transferable, worldwide licence to:</p>
+<ul>
+<li>install and use it on computers that <strong>you</strong> use (for example your desktop and your laptop);</li>
+<li>use it for personal <strong>and commercial</strong> projects.</li>
+</ul>
+<p>One purchase = one person. A studio or team needs one purchase per person who uses the Software. For a team, email us and we'll send multi-seat pricing.</p>
+<h2>2. Your videos are yours</h2>
+<p>Everything you make with the Software (videos, images, posting texts, project files) belongs to you or to whoever owns the material you put in. We claim no rights in it, and you don't owe us credit or royalties.</p>
+<h2>3. What you may not do</h2>
+<p>You may not:</p>
+<ul>
+<li>sell, rent, share, give away or re-upload the Software, its installer or your download link;</li>
+<li>share copies of the Software or let people outside the licence use it;</li>
+<li>remove or change copyright notices, or pass off the Software as your own;</li>
+<li>modify the Software and distribute the modified version;</li>
+<li>reverse-engineer it except where the law says you may;</li>
+<li>use it to break the law or anyone else's rights.</li>
+</ul>
+<h2>4. Your content and other people's rights</h2>
+<p>You are responsible for the clips, music, sounds, fonts and voices you use, and for having the rights to publish them. You must also follow the rules of the sites where you post (for example YouTube, TikTok, Instagram, X, Reddit).</p>
+<h2>5. Optional third-party services</h2>
+<p>The Software can connect to <strong>ElevenLabs</strong> to generate voice lines, but only if you enter your own API key. That service is provided by ElevenLabs under its own terms and prices, not by us. Your key is stored only on your computer. We are not responsible for third-party services, their availability or their charges.</p>
+<p>"Copy &amp; open" opens third-party websites in your browser. Their terms apply there.</p>
+<h2>6. Third-party components</h2>
+<p>The Software includes or uses open-source components (for example Python, ffmpeg, Pillow and fonts). Each comes under its own licence, listed in <strong>Third-Party Notices.txt</strong> in the download. Where those licences give you more rights than this EULA, those licences apply to those components.</p>
+<h2>7. Updates and support</h2>
+<p>We may release updates and fixes. Updates for version 1.x are free. We may change or end features in future versions. We aim to answer support requests within a day or two, but we don't guarantee a response time.</p>
+<h2>8. No warranty</h2>
+<p>The Software is provided "as is". To the extent the law allows, we make no warranties, express or implied, including fitness for a particular purpose, merchantability and non-infringement. We don't promise that it will be error-free, that it will run on every computer, or that platforms will accept every video it makes. Nothing in this section removes rights you have under consumer laws that can't be excluded.</p>
+<h2>9. Limit of liability</h2>
+<p>To the extent the law allows, we are not liable for indirect, incidental, special or consequential losses, or for lost data, profits, revenue or accounts. Our total liability for any claim about the Software is limited to the amount you paid for it. Keep backups of your projects and clips.</p>
+<h2>10. Ending the licence</h2>
+<p>This licence lasts until it ends. It ends automatically if you break this EULA. When it ends, you must stop using and delete the Software. Sections 2, 4, 8, 9 and 11 continue after it ends.</p>
+<h2>11. Law and disputes</h2>
+<p>This EULA is governed by the laws of Pakistan. The courts of Karachi, Pakistan have jurisdiction, unless consumer law where you live gives you the right to bring a claim in your own country. Before going to court, please contact us so we can try to sort it out.</p>
+<h2>12. Changes</h2>
+<p>We may update this EULA for future versions. The version that came with your copy applies to that copy.</p>
+<h2>13. Contact</h2>
